## Section 4: scientific verdict (R1680 negative verdict overturned)
The R1680 DCT parameter sweep concluded the scaling family
(0.5x/2.0x bilinear resize, direct ber 0.5195/0.5000) had NO
near-survival band inside the quantization-step x repetition grid,
and named template alignment (recover.py, W1c precedent) as the only
remaining path. This experiment confirms that path works for BOTH
cases:
  - 0.5x downscale: estimate_crop_parameters finds scale_infer=2.0
    exactly (search window (1.0,2.2), 200 samples, two refinement
    passes); canvas rebuild + resize-back yields ber 0.5195 -> 0.0547
    (inside the 0.10 near-survival band = RECOVERED).
  - 2.0x upscale: scale_infer=0.5 exactly; resize-back to the original
    canvas yields ber 0.5000 -> 0.0000 (bit-exact = RECOVERED).
Direct readings reproduce the R1680 recorded values exactly
(0.5195/0.5000), closing the cross-check loop.
Production note (bootstrap window): the verifier needs the embedded
original for template matching (same assumption as the W1c crop
case); the scale search makes recovery robust to unknown scale
factors within the searched range, not only the two probe points.
